For \(n,d\in\mathbb N\) and \(0<\epsilon\le 1/2\), the overlap-restricted iid product-law experiment class associated with \cref{obj:ass:iid-sampling,obj:ass:overlap} is
\[
\mathcal E_{n,d,\epsilon}
:=
\left\{
P^{\otimes n}:
P\in\mathsf{Prob}(\{1,\ldots,d\}\times\{0,1\}^2)
\text{ and } P \text{ satisfies the overlap condition}
\right\}.
\]

Define the minimax mean-squared-error risk by
\[
\mathsf R_{n,d,\epsilon}
=
\inf_{\widehat\tau}
\sup_{P^{\otimes n}\in\mathcal E_{n,d,\epsilon}}
E_P\!\left[(\widehat\tau-\tau(P))^2\right],
\]
where the infimum ranges over all measurable estimators \(\widehat\tau\) based on \(O_1,\ldots,O_n\).
